<overview>
<p>The Combine's martial traditions extend beyond the BattleMech cockpit, and the Dictum Honorium demands that all citizens contribute their talents to the defense of House Kurita. Infantry soldiers of the DCMS embody that expectation on garrison worlds across the realm. Tracked mechanized infantry ride armored carriers that can cross rough ground where wheeled vehicles cannot follow. The DCMS values these platoons for operations on worlds with poor road infrastructure, where the broken terrain that stops lighter transport is simply another day's march for tracked APCs and the soldiers they carry. Armed with standard assault rifles, the cheapest and most widely manufactured personal weapon in the Inner Sphere. Effective range is limited, but any world with basic industry can produce and stockpile them in quantity, and resupply is rarely a concern even on remote garrison posts. These sappers specialize in demolition, obstacle construction, and field fortification. Whether preparing defensive positions before the enemy arrives or breaching obstacles during an advance, they shape the ground that everyone else fights on.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on introduction date of ballistic plate armor. Ballistic plate armor chosen for damage divisor and ATOW stats and general description.
</notes>

